{
  "topic": "doom_cartoons",
  "ttsScript": "MF DOOM sampled Fantastic Four cartoons on almost every album. People thought it was a gimmick. But Daniel Dumile and his brother grew up sharing a clock radio in Long Beach, recording hip hop on cassette tapes, reading comic books together. In 1993, his brother was killed crossing a highway. He was nineteen. Elektra dropped their group. Dumile went homeless. When he came back, he wore a mask modeled on Doctor Doom, a villain who built a machine to contact the dead. Every cartoon sample was a portal back to a bedroom where his brother was still alive. DOOM said there is no more after 1993. So he built a world entirely out of before.",
